    "https://www.sjny.edu/employment/job/11077": {
      "title": "Lead Teachers for our UPK Programs",
      "description": "Lead Teachers for our UPK Programs | St. Joseph's University, New York Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Lead Teachers for our UPK Programs October 16, 2026 Long Island Campus Universal Prekindergarten Program Freeport SD, Lawrence SD, Plainedge SD, Uniondale SD and Westbury SD The St. Joseph's University Universal Prekindergarten Programs is seeking Lead Teachers for our UPK Programs. St Joseph’s UPK provides high quality prekindergarten services to 5 districts in Long Island. St. Joseph's UPK utilizes the Co-teaching model and this experience will count toward professional hours for NYS Certifications. Salaries for Lead Teachers are around $230 per day. No benefits are offered. This position is part time, follows the district school calendar and pre-k school day. Duties and Responsibilities Planning, developing, and implementing the age-appropriate curriculum. Devising and imparting lesson plans on a daily basis Set up interest centers and prepare instructional material. Instruct and supervise children in social and developmental activities Supervise students within the classroom and during recreational activities. Provide an environment of comfort and security for young students by indulging in nurturing behavior. Guide and help handle remedial work activities in either small groups or 1:1. Assist students during lunchtime, toileting, and washing activities. Enforce cleanup activities after centers and lunchtime by modeling appropriate behavior and reinforcement songs. Observe students for changes in behavior and report findings to your co teacher, site supervisor and director. Evaluate students with informal and formal assessments. Supervise students during field trips to ensure their safety and wellbeing. Organize and supervise gross motor activities during outdoor/indoor recess. Collaborate with Site Supervisor about student record keeping, filing, teacher made materials and photocopying activities. Provide input on the overall progress of a student consistently and during parent-teacher meetings/conferences. Provide one-on-one support to young students, such as helping them write their names or learning initial counting. Requirements NYSED Teacher Certification in N-6 or B-2 (Masters preferred) At least 6 credits in a Master Program toward education. Experience working with children in a school or recreational setting Application Process and Additional Information If you are ready to share your love of teaching and adoration of young children in a high quality pre-kindergarten environment, please send resumes and letters of intent to Mrs. Pamela Renneisen, Director of St. Joseph's UPK Programs at prenneisen@sjny.edu Mail For - Application Process and Additional Information . It is the policy of St. Joseph's University not to discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, citizenship, age, disability, genetic information, status as a victim of domestic violence, military status, status as a protected veteran, marital status or status of an individual in any group or class protected by applicable federal, New York State or New York City Law. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, and all other school administered programs or policies. The University also provides accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in accordance with the Americans With Disabilities Act and applicable state and local laws. If you need an accommodation during the application process or while employed, please contact Human Resources. Your employment is contingent upon receipt of proof of eligibility to work in the United States. Please note that the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) requires that all U.S. employers complete and retain a current Form I-9 for each individual they hire for employment in the United States, verifying the employment eligibility and identity documents presented by the employee and recording the document information. You will be required to complete your portion of the document, with your documentation verifying your identity and eligibility to work, no later than your third day of employment. Get Social Get Social Esse non videri — “To be, not to seem.” The mission of St. Joseph’s University is to provide a strong academic and value-oriented education at the undergraduate and graduate levels, rooted in a liberal arts tradition that supports provision for career preparation and enhancement. READ OUR FULL MISSION. BROOKLYN 245 Clinton Ave., Brooklyn, NY 11205 Addess For - BROOKLYN Main: 718.940.5300 Admissions: 718.940.5800 Fax: 718.940.5680 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy LONG ISLAND 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - LONG ISLAND Main: 631.687.5100 Admissions: 631.687.4500 Fax: 631.687.4539 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy ONLINE 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - ONLINE 631.687.4501 Home Programs Admissions FAQs Affordability Credit for Experience Military & Veterans Library Privacy Policy Sitemap | Accessibility Statement Opens in new window PDF Download Word Download Excel Download PowerPoint Download Document Download Explore your accessibility options"
