    "https://www.sjny.edu/employment/job/11032": {
      "title": "Adjunct Physics Instructor-Chemistry and Physical Sciences",
      "description": "Adjunct Physics Instructor-Chemistry and Physical Sciences | St. Joseph's University, New York Skip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\". Adjunct Physics Instructor-Chemistry and Physical Sciences September 9, 2026 Brooklyn Campus Chemistry and Physical Sciences The Chemistry and Physical Sciences Department at St. Joseph’s University, Brooklyn, NY, is seeking an adjunct instructor for the following course for the Spring 2027 semester (1/25/27 – 5/12/27): Course Description This course provides an introduction to the fundamental principles of electricity, magnetism, and optics. Topics include electrostatics, electric currents, direct-current circuits, magnetism, magnetic induction, alternating-current circuits, and electromagnetism. The course also examines electromagnetic waves and the nature and propagation of light, including reflection, refraction, mirrors, lenses, optical instruments, interference, diffraction, and polarization. The course emphasizes developing conceptual understanding and applying physical principles to solve quantitative problems involving electrical, magnetic, and optical systems. Lecture : Mon, Wed, 9:05 - 10:30 a.m. Lab : Mon, 1:40 - 4:40 p.m. Recitation for PHY 161 (General Physics II- Calculus Based): Mon 4:40 - 5:30 p.m. Requirements A master’s degree in physics or a related field and experience in teaching higher education are required. Application Process and Additional Information Salary : approximately $1000 per credit hour Qualified applicants should send a CV, list of courses taught, and contact information for 2 references to Jeonghee Kang Ph.D., Chemistry and Physical Sciences Department Chair , at jkang@sjny.edu Mail For - Application Process and Additional Information . It is the policy of St. Joseph's University not to discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, citizenship, age, disability, genetic information, status as a victim of domestic violence, military status, status as a protected veteran, marital status or status of an individual in any group or class protected by applicable federal, New York State or New York City Law. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, educational programs, admissions policies, financial aid, and all other school administered programs or policies. The University also provides accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in accordance with the Americans With Disabilities Act and applicable state and local laws. If you need an accommodation during the application process or while employed, please contact Human Resources. Your employment is contingent upon receipt of proof of eligibility to work in the United States. Please note that the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) requires that all U.S. employers complete and retain a current Form I-9 for each individual they hire for employment in the United States, verifying the employment eligibility and identity documents presented by the employee and recording the document information. You will be required to complete your portion of the document, with your documentation verifying your identity and eligibility to work, no later than your third day of employment. Get Social Get Social Esse non videri — “To be, not to seem.” The mission of St. Joseph’s University is to provide a strong academic and value-oriented education at the undergraduate and graduate levels, rooted in a liberal arts tradition that supports provision for career preparation and enhancement. READ OUR FULL MISSION. BROOKLYN 245 Clinton Ave., Brooklyn, NY 11205 Addess For - BROOKLYN Main: 718.940.5300 Admissions: 718.940.5800 Fax: 718.940.5680 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy LONG ISLAND 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - LONG ISLAND Main: 631.687.5100 Admissions: 631.687.4500 Fax: 631.687.4539 Home About Admissions Academics Student Life Library Athletics Alumni Giving MySJNY Privacy Policy ONLINE 155 W. Roe Blvd., Patchogue, NY 11772 Addess For - ONLINE 631.687.4501 Home Programs Admissions FAQs Affordability Credit for Experience Military & Veterans Library Privacy Policy Sitemap | Accessibility Statement Opens in new window PDF Download Word Download Excel Download PowerPoint Download Document Download Explore your accessibility options"
